    overview: "Plaza Hamabar is a small, quiet plaza located near the Cebu Metropolitan Cathedral. It features a large statue of Rajah Humabon (also known as Hamabar), the pre-colonial ruler of Cebu who welcomed Magellan's expedition in 1521. The plaza is a simple green space with benches and a few commemorative plaques explaining the ruler's significance.\n\nVisitors can stop by for a brief rest while walking between the Cathedral and the Parian district. It is much less crowded than the nearby Plaza Sugbo, offering a more tranquil environment to reflect on the early history of the city and its pre-colonial leadership.",
