    name: "Fuente Osmeña Circle",
    description: "A historic rotunda and public park that serves as the heart of midtown Cebu City.",
    overview: "Fuente Osmeña Circle is a circular public park and fountain located at the intersection of Osmeña Boulevard and other major roads in midtown Cebu. The park features a landmark fountain built in 1912 to commemorate the city's new water system. It is a green oasis in the middle of a busy commercial district, with wide paths, benches, and manicured gardens.\n\nVisitors will find it a central landmark for navigating the city. During the day, it is a pleasant spot for a stroll or to sit and watch the traffic pass by. At night, especially during the Christmas season and the Sinulog festival, the circle is brilliantly illuminated and becomes a hub for outdoor events, concerts, and night markets. It is the geographic center of the city's social and commercial life outside the downtown area.",
    significance: "Fuente Osmeña is significant as a symbol of the city's modernization and its entry into the 20th century. Named after Sergio Osmeña, the first Filipino Speaker of the House and later President of the Philippines, it honors one of Cebu's greatest sons. The fountain itself represents the city's growth and its ability to provide modern infrastructure for its citizens.\n\nCulturally, the circle is the ground zero for many of Cebu's most important public celebrations. It is a traditional gathering point for student groups, sports enthusiasts, and families. The preservation of this rotunda is vital for the city's identity and its urban layout, linking the old downtown with the growing uptown districts.",
