    description: "The seat of the local government, overlooking Plaza Sugbo and the historical district.",
    overview: "Cebu City Hall is a prominent government building located across from Plaza Sugbo and Magellan's Cross. The current structure is a blend of classical and modern architectural styles, serving as the administrative headquarters for the city. Its location puts it right at the heart of the city's most historic zone, making it a visible symbol of civic authority.\n\nVisitors can appreciate the building's facade from the plaza or enter the lobby to see the various city departments in action. The area around the City Hall is a busy hub of activity, with people from all walks of life conducting official business or exploring the nearby landmarks. It is a landmark that represents the continuity of governance in the Philippines' oldest city.",
