    description: "A colorful temple and major cultural landmark for the local Chinese community.",
    overview: "The Cebu Taoist Temple is a magnificent place of worship located in the Beverly Hills subdivision of Cebu City. Built in 1972, the temple sits at an elevation of 300 meters above sea level. It is characterized by its colorful multi-tiered roofs, dragon motifs, and intricate carvings that follow traditional Chinese architectural styles. The complex includes several temples, a small replica of the Great Wall of China, and beautifully landscaped gardens.\n\nVisitors can climb the 81 steps (representing the 81 chapters of Taoist scripture) to reach the main temple and enjoy a panoramic view of Cebu City and Mactan Island. The atmosphere is serene and respectful, as it is still an active place of worship. It is a popular destination for those seeking peace, beautiful architecture, and a wider perspective of the city's cultural diversity.",
