    description: "The historic beach where American liberation forces landed in 1945 to free Cebu.",
    overview: "The Talisay Landing Site, located at Larawan Beach, is a major WWII memorial in Talisay City. It features several large statues depicting the American liberation forces wading ashore from their landing crafts on March 26, 1945. The site is an open beach area with a memorial park that includes historical markers and plaques explaining the details of the military operation.\n\nVisitors can see the monument up close and walk along the beach where the actual landing took place. It is a place of reflection, often used for commemorative ceremonies every March. The park offers a scenic view of the sea and serves as a vital historical lesson for those interested in the role of Cebu in the Pacific theater of WWII.",
