    description: "A historic public square and the center of community life in Talisay.",
    overview: "Talisay City Plaza is a wide open public space located in front of the Sta. Teresa de Avila Church and near the old city hall. It is a traditional Filipino town plaza with paved walks, benches, and a central stage or kiosk. The plaza is surrounded by trees and offers a refreshing space for people to gather and relax.\n\nVisitors will see children playing, students studying, and locals chatting in the park. It is a great place to experience the local lifestyle of Talisay. The plaza is the venue for many city-wide events, such as the Inasal Festival and various civic celebrations. It remains the social heart of the city's downtown district.",
