    overview: "The Suico Ancestral House is a private heritage residence located in Mandaue City. It is an excellent example of the traditional Filipino house design that bridge the gap between the Spanish colonial and American styles. The house features wide windows with capiz shells, high ceilings for natural ventilation, and intricate wooden carvings. It sits on a well-maintained property that reflects the lifestyle of a prominent Mandaue family.\n\nWhile it is a private home, its exterior can be appreciated from the street, and it is a well-known landmark for locals interested in heritage. The house is a reminder of the residential character of Mandaue before it became a major industrial center. It stands as a silent witness to the history and domestic traditions of the city.",
